The `vaca` skill in plugins/rancho/skills/vaca is derived from CCPM, from the
`/pm:*` slash-command generation of that project (preserved upstream on its
`v1` branch).
The spec-driven delivery workflow it implements — product requirement document
to technical epic to GitHub issues to parallel agents — originates there, as do
the `.claude/prds/` and `.claude/epics/` layout, the task frontmatter schema,
the dependency and parallelisation model, the tracking scripts, and the use of
the `gh-sub-issue` GitHub CLI extension.

The material has been substantially modified: the command surface was replaced
with natural-language triggers, frontmatter parsing was consolidated into a
single set of awk readers, and the workflow was bound to the engineering law
carried by the `law` skill.

